@page "/demo/ribbon"
@using FlexCore.Showcase.Components.Shared

@* 2026-10-29: own page for the ribbon. Facts from Ribbon*.razor and RibbonControl.razor.css (FlexCore 0.2.50): first tab open on
   load; only the open tab's groups render; Icon prints as text.
   2026-11-14: fuller examples (four tabs, a dropdown button, a group of check boxes, a hide and show button, toggles, a disabled
   group, a hidden tab) on the library's ribbon work of the same day: tab roles and arrow keys, Collapsible, Pressed,
   DropDownContent, Visible and Disabled on tabs and groups, wrapping when narrow. *@

<PageTitle>Blazor Ribbon Control — FlexCore</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Ribbon" Category="Components" ControlName="RibbonControl"
                   Tagline="Organize many commands into tabs and titled groups, Office style."
                   SourcePath="RibbonControl.razor;RibbonTab.razor;RibbonGroup.razor;RibbonButton.razor;RibbonControl.razor.css">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>RibbonControl</code> is a Blazor ribbon: an Office-style command bar with tabs across the top and titled groups of large and small buttons in each. Use it when a screen has more commands than a toolbar can hold, such as editing a booking; only the open tab's groups are shown, so the bar stays compact. The buttons hold no state, so your page decides what each does, when it is disabled and how it looks pressed.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="tabs" Title="A booking desk ribbon" RazorCode="@Code.Tabs" CSharpCode="@Code.TabsCs" CssCode="@Code.TabsCss">
            <Description><p>Work the four tabs: Cut or Copy enables Paste, Email opens a <code>DropDownContent</code> menu, and one group holds check boxes instead of buttons. Hide the ribbon with the arrow on the right or a double-click on a tab; Reports is a <code>Disabled</code> tab.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="desk-ribbon">
                    <RibbonControl Collapsible="true" @bind-Collapsed="_hidden">
                        <RibbonTab Title="Home">
                            <RibbonGroup Title="Clipboard">
                                <RibbonButton Text="Paste" Icon="📋" Large="true" Disabled="@(_clipboard is null)" OnClick="@(() => Did($"Pasted {_clipboard}"))" />
                                <RibbonButton Text="Cut" Icon="✂️" OnClick="@(() => Clip("Cut"))" />
                                <RibbonButton Text="Copy" Icon="📄" OnClick="@(() => Clip("Copied"))" />
                            </RibbonGroup>
                            <RibbonGroup Title="Booking">
                                <RibbonButton Text="New booking" Icon="🧳" Large="true" OnClick="@(() => Did("Started a new booking"))" />
                                <RibbonButton Text="Hold" Icon="⏸️" Tooltip="Hold the seats for 24 hours" OnClick="@(() => Did("Held the seats"))" />
                                <RibbonButton Text="Duplicate" Icon="🗂️" OnClick="@(() => Did("Duplicated the booking"))" />
                                <RibbonButton Text="Cancel" Icon="✖️" OnClick="@(() => Did("Canceled the booking"))" />
                            </RibbonGroup>
                            <RibbonGroup>
                                <div class="ribbon-options">
                                    <CheckBoxControl @bind-Checked="_showCanceled" Label="Show canceled" />
                                    <CheckBoxControl @bind-Checked="_autoSave" Label="Save as I go" />
                                </div>
                            </RibbonGroup>
                        </RibbonTab>
                        <RibbonTab Title="Trip">
                            <RibbonGroup Title="Flights">
                                <RibbonButton Text="Add flight" Icon="✈️" Large="true" OnClick="@(() => Did("Added a flight"))" />
                                <RibbonButton Text="Change" Icon="🔁" OnClick="@(() => Did("Changed the flight"))" />
                                <RibbonButton Text="Seats" Icon="💺" OnClick="@(() => Did("Opened the seat map"))" />
                            </RibbonGroup>
                            <RibbonGroup Title="Stay">
                                <RibbonButton Text="Add hotel" Icon="🏨" Large="true" OnClick="@(() => Did("Added a hotel"))" />
                                <RibbonButton Text="Upgrade" Icon="⭐" OnClick="@(() => Did("Upgraded the room"))" />
                            </RibbonGroup>
                            <RibbonGroup Title="Extras">
                                <RibbonButton Text="Transfer" Icon="🚐" OnClick="@(() => Did("Added an airport transfer"))" />
                                <RibbonButton Text="Insurance" Icon="🛡️" OnClick="@(() => Did("Added travel insurance"))" />
                                <RibbonButton Text="Excursion" Icon="🗺️" OnClick="@(() => Did("Added an excursion"))" />
                            </RibbonGroup>
                        </RibbonTab>
                        <RibbonTab Title="Documents">
                            <RibbonGroup Title="Send">
                                <RibbonButton @ref="_send" Text="Email" Icon="✉️" Large="true">
                                    <DropDownContent>
                                        @foreach (var doc in new[] { "Itinerary", "Invoice", "Tickets" })
                                        {
                                            <ButtonControl BareStyle="true" CssClass="ribbon-menu-item" OnClick="@(() => Send(doc))">@doc</ButtonControl>
                                        }
                                    </DropDownContent>
                                </RibbonButton>
                                <RibbonButton Text="Print" Icon="🖨️" OnClick="@(() => Did("Printed the itinerary"))" />
                                <RibbonButton Text="Download" Icon="⬇️" OnClick="@(() => Did("Downloaded the documents"))" />
                            </RibbonGroup>
                        </RibbonTab>
                        <RibbonTab Title="Reports" Disabled="true" />
                    </RibbonControl>
                </div>
                <span class="result">@(_last ?? "Click a button, open another tab, or hide the ribbon with the arrow on the right.")</span>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="pressed" Title="Toggles, disabled groups and hidden tabs" RazorCode="@Code.Pressed" CSharpCode="@Code.PressedCs" CssCode="@Code.PressedCss">
            <Description><p>Bold, Italic and Highlight are toggles through <code>Pressed</code>. Lock the text to disable both groups with <code>Disabled</code>, and show the Review tab with <code>Visible</code>.</p></Description>
            <Controls>
                <ToggleButtonControl @bind-Selected="_locked">Lock the text</ToggleButtonControl>
                <ToggleButtonControl @bind-Selected="_review">Show the Review tab</ToggleButtonControl>
            </Controls>
            <Demo>
                <div class="paper-ribbon">
                    <RibbonControl CssClass="paper">
                        <RibbonTab Title="Format">
                            <RibbonGroup Title="Style" Disabled="@_locked">
                                <RibbonButton Text="Bold" Icon="B" Pressed="@_bold" OnClick="@(() => _bold = !_bold)" />
                                <RibbonButton Text="Italic" Icon="I" Pressed="@_italic" OnClick="@(() => _italic = !_italic)" />
                                <RibbonButton Text="Highlight" Icon="🖍️" Pressed="@_highlight" OnClick="@(() => _highlight = !_highlight)" />
                            </RibbonGroup>
                            <RibbonGroup Title="Text size" Disabled="@_locked">
                                <RibbonButton Text="Larger" Icon="A+" Disabled="@(_size >= 22)" OnClick="@(() => _size += 2)" />
                                <RibbonButton Text="Smaller" Icon="A−" Disabled="@(_size <= 12)" OnClick="@(() => _size -= 2)" />
                            </RibbonGroup>
                        </RibbonTab>
                        <RibbonTab Title="Review" Visible="@_review">
                            <RibbonGroup Title="Check">
                                <RibbonButton Text="Spelling" Icon="✔️" Large="true" OnClick="@(() => _checked = "No spelling mistakes found.")" />
                                <RibbonButton Text="Word count" Icon="🔢" OnClick="@(() => _checked = "17 words.")" />
                            </RibbonGroup>
                        </RibbonTab>
                    </RibbonControl>
                </div>
                <p class="note-text @(_bold ? "bold" : "") @(_italic ? "italic" : "") @(_highlight ? "highlight" : "")" style="font-size:@(_size)px">
                    Meet the group at the old town gate at nine. Bring water, a hat and comfortable shoes.
                </p>
                <span class="result">@_checked</span>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <DocSections>
            <DocSection Id="doc-ribbon" Title="RibbonControl" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Ribbon.Length, "parameters")' Open="true">
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="RibbonControl" Rows="Vocab.Ribbon" />
                <p class="note">Tabs join the strip in the order they first render: there is no parameter or method to open a tab from code, and a tab removed from the page later keeps its header, so hide a tab with <code>Visible</code> instead. The four components accept no attributes beyond the parameters listed here.</p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-tab" Title="RibbonTab" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Tab.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="RibbonTab" Rows="Vocab.Tab" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-group" Title="RibbonGroup" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Group.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="RibbonGroup" Rows="Vocab.Group" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-button" Title="RibbonButton" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Button.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="RibbonButton" Rows="Vocab.Button" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-css-classes" Title="CSS classes" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Css.Length, "classes")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssClasses" Title="CSS classes" Rows="Vocab.Css" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-css-variables" Title="CSS variables" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Vars.Length, "variables")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssVariables" Title="CSS variables" Rows="Vocab.Vars" />
                <p class="note">The other colors, the borders and the spacing are fixed in the control's stylesheet.</p>
            </DocSection>
        </DocSections>
    </Vocabulary>

    <Accessibility>
        <ul>
            <li>The tab strip is a <code>tablist</code> of native buttons with <code>role="tab"</code> and <code>aria-selected</code>; the open tab's groups sit in a <code>tabpanel</code> named by its tab. The tabs share one Tab stop: Left and Right move to the next tab that can be opened, Home and End to the first and last. With <code>Collapsible</code>, the hide and show button is a second Tab stop inside the <code>tablist</code>; it carries <code>aria-expanded</code> and the label "Show the ribbon" or "Hide the ribbon".</li>
            <li>Each <code>RibbonButton</code> is a native <code>&lt;button type="button"&gt;</code>, so Tab reaches it and Enter or Space runs it. Its <code>title</code> is the tooltip, or the label when there is none. A toggle carries <code>aria-pressed</code>. A dropdown button carries <code>aria-haspopup</code> and <code>aria-expanded</code>, and no <code>aria-pressed</code> even when <code>Pressed</code> is set.</li>
            <li>A group is a <code>role="group"</code> named by its <code>Title</code>.</li>
            <li>The glyph is plain text inside the button, so a screen reader reads an emoji glyph before the label.</li>
            <li>A dropdown panel closes on a click outside it. There is no Escape or arrow-key handling inside the panel.</li>
        </ul>
    </Accessibility>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li>A single row of commands: <a href="demo/toolbar">Toolbar</a>.</li>
            <li>Tabs that switch page content: <a href="demo/tabs-accordion#tabs">Tabs &amp; accordion</a>.</li>
            <li>Plain buttons, with a dropdown mode: <a href="demo/buttons">Buttons</a>.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

